5,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,I believe we should prioritize stability and reliability. I would like to look into the winter road closures north of the river and the bus links in the two outer wards.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Yumi,,"That sounds like a great start, Ryuji! I'm really interested in how people actually get to us. I'll look into the bus links in the two outer wards and the attendance sheets from former outreach stops!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,George,,"I agree that accessibility is key. However, I am concerned about the long-term financial structure. I will look into the county grant terms and the endowment, as well as the running and equipment lines last year.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,May,,Everyone is so focused on the future! I think we should see what actually happened in the past. I'll look into the two programmes begun six years ago and the attendance sheets from former outreach stops.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I think it's important to know if we have enough help. I'll look into the volunteer register and supervision training, and... the neighbourhood associations and tool certification.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,It seems we have a broad range of interests. I am curious if anyone else feels that our current operations are too vulnerable to external factors beyond our immediate control.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Yumi,,I totally get that! It's scary to think that something as simple as a road closure or a bus schedule could stop someone from visiting. We should definitely make sure everyone can reach us easily!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,George,,"While accessibility is important, we must ensure the funding is sustainable. If the financial foundation is unstable, even the best transport links won't save a program in the long run.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,May,,"@George, you're so serious! But really, why guess about sustainability when we have records? I bet we've already tried ""sustainable"" ideas that flopped. Let's see if history has any lessons for us first.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree that history is useful. But I'm just worried that if we start something new, the staff might be too overwhelmed. I hope we can find a way to support them.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, your concern about staff capacity is valid. However, if we ignore the external variables that disrupt our schedules, we risk overloading the staff with failed initiatives. We must ensure the plan is resilient.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, you're so right! If we can figure out the best ways for people to get here, it'll make everything run smoother for the staff too. Let's make sure no one gets left behind!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,George,,"I appreciate the enthusiasm, but we must not overlook the structural side of things. A resilient plan requires a financial framework that doesn't crumble after a year. Let us see what the data reveals first.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,May,,"@George, you're treating this like a math problem! Data is great, but only if you're looking at the right data. I'm more interested in the ghosts of projects past than a spreadsheet of grants.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I just don't want anyone to get burned out. I hope the volunteer register shows we have enough people to help, so the staff don't have to do everything themselves.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Ryuji,,"It seems we have a consensus on the need for a comprehensive view. I will stick with my choices to assess external risks, as stability is the prerequisite for any successful expansion.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Yumi,,"I'm with you, Ryuji! I'll stick with my choices too. I really want to see who we've been reaching and how we can make it even easier for everyone to join in! Let's do this!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,George,,I shall also remain with my selections. Understanding the nature of our funding is the only way to ensure we don't overextend ourselves. I look forward to seeing the results.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,May,,I'll stick with mine too. I'm dying to see what those old programs were and why they're gathering dust. Let's hope the past gives us a little more excitement than a budget report!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'll stick with my choices too. I just hope we can find a way to make sure the people working here are okay. I'll see what I can find out.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
