35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The data confirms my fears. The loss of bus links has created a significant barrier for residents, and while community halls managed, our reliance on external transport makes our services fragile. We need a solution that doesn't depend on these variables.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Oh no, that's terrible! People in the outer wards have to travel an hour just to reach us? And they used to come in such big numbers! We absolutely have to find a way to get back to them!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"My findings confirm a structural flaw. The grant only covers the first year, leaving the operating budget to struggle later. Furthermore, we are mismanaging funds, letting equipment budgets lapse while running costs spiral. We must address this.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"It's just as I thought! We have these ""ghosts"" in the system. One project was a total mess, but another is still running perfectly without any help. Why are we ignoring what actually works?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found something worrying. We have volunteers, but no staff are trained to supervise them. Also, the person who certified our power tools retired. I'm afraid we don't have the actual skills on staff to manage new things.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, that is a critical point. Between the lack of supervision training and the transport failures, we are operating on a foundation of luck. We cannot propose an expansion that relies on unstable transport or untrained staff.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, I agree that we can't rely on luck, but we can't just give up on those people! If they can't get to us, we have to bring the library to them. It's not fair!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, bringing the library to them sounds noble, but look at the ledger. Our vehicle running costs already overran by a third last year. We cannot expand outreach if we cannot afford the fuel.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@George, you're still staring at the pennies! We have a partner-run group that's been thriving for six years without a dime of our budget. Why not just copy that model instead of fighting over fuel costs?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think May might be right. If we use a model where others help lead, maybe the staff won't be so overwhelmed. But we still need someone who can actually supervise them...","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, a partner-run model could reduce our dependence on county transport and budgets. However, @Daisuke's point remains: without supervision training, we are simply shifting the risk. We need a plan that is both autonomous and properly managed.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, @Daisuke, you're both right! But we can't forget those people in the outer wards. If we find a way to train supervisors and use May's partner model, we can reach them without breaking the bank!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Daisuke"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Yumi, your optimism is noted, but we must be realistic. If the grant only covers the first year, any new ""partner model"" will eventually drain our operating budget. We need a plan with a sustainable funding structure.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@George, you're such a killjoy! If a group has survived six years unaided, it's already proven it doesn't need your precious budget. Why keep inventing ""sustainable"" plans when we have a living example of one?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I just worry that even a partner model puts pressure on the staff to coordinate everything. If we don't have the training to supervise, it might just create more stress for them in the end.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"We must prioritize a model that minimizes external dependencies. If we can implement a partner-led system that operates independently of our transport and budget, while simultaneously addressing the supervision gap, we achieve true stability.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I totally agree! Let's find a way to bring the library back to the outer wards using that partner model. If we can fix the supervision part, we can help everyone without worrying about the buses!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"I will concede that a partner-led model is promising, provided it does not create a hidden financial burden. However, we must ensure the proposal includes a clear plan for supervision training to avoid the risks @Daisuke mentioned.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,Finally! It only took a few rounds of arguing for you all to see the light. Let's just stop overthinking and pick the one that actually works in the real world. I'm ready to vote!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm glad we're thinking about the staff. If the proposal we choose includes training and doesn't just add more work to their plates, then I think I can support it. I'll do my best.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
