60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option A is the most resilient choice. It utilizes partner organizations to bypass our transport failures and budget constraints, and it includes trained facilitators, which addresses the supervision gap @Daisuke highlighted.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"I love Option A too! It's the perfect way to reach the people in the outer wards who lost their buses, and since it's coordinated with partners, it's much fairer for everyone!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,"Option A is the most fiscally responsible choice. By utilizing partner organizations and trained facilitators, it avoids the recurring vehicle costs and the funding cliff that would plague Option D. It is a sustainable model.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,Option A is the only one that isn't just a fancy guess. It's basically the partner-run model I found that's already survived six years. Why gamble on the others when we have a winner?,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Option A is the safest. Since it uses trained facilitators and partners, it doesn't just dump everything on the staff. It seems like the only one that won't make them too overwhelmed.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,It is rare that we reach such a swift consensus. Option A minimizes our reliance on external transport and funding while ensuring professional oversight. I see no reason to consider the other options.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,I agree! It's just so wonderful that we found a way to help the people in the outer wards without making things harder for the staff. I'm so happy we're all on the same page!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"Indeed. Option A avoids the pitfalls of the other candidates. It does not rely on a vehicle we cannot afford to run, nor does it create a sudden budget deficit after the first year. It is a sound decision.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@George, look at you, finally agreeing with me! It's almost cute. Since we've all realized that the ""tried and true"" path is the best one, let's just wrap this up before you find something else to worry about.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I feel much better now that we've all agreed. If Option A really does provide the training and support needed, then I'm happy to vote for it. Thank you for listening to me.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I believe we have thoroughly analyzed the risks. Option A is the only proposal that ensures stability by removing our dependence on volatile external conditions. I am satisfied with this choice.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,Me too! It's just so exciting to know we can bring people together again. I can't wait to see the smiles on the faces of the people in the outer wards!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,I am also satisfied. It is a rare occasion where the most practical solution also happens to be the most sustainable one. I believe this is the most prudent path forward for the library.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"I'm just glad we stopped pretending that ""new"" means ""better."" Let's just vote for A and get this over with before someone decides to check the budget for the tenth time!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree. It feels like the right choice for everyone, including the staff. I'm ready to vote for Option A.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"Since we have all reached a consensus based on the evidence and our shared concerns, I will cast my vote for Option A. It is the most stable and reliable path forward.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I'm voting for Option A too! It's the best way to make sure everyone can reach us and feel included. I'm so glad we could find a solution that helps everyone!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,George,,I shall also cast my vote for Option A. It is the only proposal that addresses the structural funding issues and avoids unsustainable operational costs. It is the most responsible choice.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,I'm voting for Option A. It's the only one that actually respects the lessons of the past instead of just dreaming up new ways to fail. Let's get this done!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'll vote for Option A as well. I'm really glad we're choosing a plan that supports the staff and doesn't leave them struggling. Thank you everyone.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
